{"term":"submissie","lang":"nl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"kink_paraphilia","subcategory":"submission","concept":"bdsm_submission","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"clinical","crude":25,"technical":55,"recognition_pct_current":88,"recognition_pct_peak":88,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Submission; in BDSM contexts, the act or role of yielding power and control to a dominant partner.","english_term":"submission","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Latin-derived; the native Dutch alternative 'onderdanigheid' (subservience) is equally used; 'submissie' carries a slightly more deliberate and chosen quality in kink discourse, implying an active decision rather than a personality trait."}
{"term":"sadisme","lang":"nl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"kink_paraphilia","subcategory":"sadism","concept":"sadism","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"clinical","crude":40,"technical":65,"recognition_pct_current":92,"recognition_pct_peak":92,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Sadism; sexual and psychological gratification derived from inflicting pain, humiliation, or suffering on another person.","english_term":"sadism","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Named after the Marquis de Sade; used both clinically (DSM-adjacent) and colloquially in Dutch; has non-sexual applications (political sadisme, organizational sadisme) that dilute its taboo charge outside BDSM contexts."}
{"term":"masochisme","lang":"nl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"kink_paraphilia","subcategory":"masochism","concept":"masochism","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"clinical","crude":40,"technical":65,"recognition_pct_current":92,"recognition_pct_peak":92,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Masochism; sexual or psychological gratification derived from experiencing pain, humiliation, or subjugation.","english_term":"masochism","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Named after Leopold von Sacher-Masoch; 'masochistisch' is used loosely in everyday Dutch for self-defeating behavior (e.g. 'dat is masochistisch'), which reduces the word's sexual charge in general usage."}
{"term":"sadomasochisme","lang":"nl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"kink_paraphilia","subcategory":"sadomasochism","concept":"sadomasochism","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"clinical","crude":55,"technical":60,"recognition_pct_current":88,"recognition_pct_peak":88,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Sadomasochism; a sexual orientation or practice encompassing both the infliction and reception of pain or humiliation for erotic gratification.","english_term":"sadomasochism","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Often abbreviated to 'SM' or 'S&M' in Dutch casual and kink-community use; the full form is formal and clinical; closely associated with the BDSM acronym in contemporary discourse."}
