{"term":"rollenspel","lang":"nl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"kink_paraphilia","subcategory":"roleplay","concept":"sexual_roleplay","is_novel_concept":true,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":35,"technical":20,"recognition_pct_current":95,"recognition_pct_peak":95,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Role play; the enactment of fictional personas or scenarios during sexual activity for arousal or fantasy fulfillment.","english_term":"role play","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"'Rollenspel' is a general Dutch word also used in therapy, education, management training, and gaming; the sexual meaning is entirely context-dependent and not inherently crude; the non-sexual frequency of the word keeps its recognition near-universal."}
{"term":"zweep","lang":"nl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"kink_paraphilia","subcategory":"impact_implement","concept":"bdsm_flogger","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":40,"technical":10,"recognition_pct_current":97,"recognition_pct_peak":97,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Whip; a single-tailed striking implement used in BDSM impact play, or any whip in general contexts such as riding or driving.","english_term":"whip","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Mapped to bdsm_flogger as the closest registry concept for BDSM impact implements; a zweep is technically a single-tail whip, distinct from a multi-tail flogger ('flogger' in Dutch kink communities); the distinction matters within BDSM but is lost on general audiences. Primary meaning for most Dutch speakers is non-sexual."}
{"term":"slaaf","lang":"nl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"kink_paraphilia","subcategory":"bdsm_submissive","concept":"bdsm_submissive","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":45,"technical":10,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Slave (masculine); in BDSM contexts, a submissive partner in a master/slave total-power-exchange dynamic who has surrendered broad authority to their dominant.","english_term":"slave","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"'Slaaf' is the ordinary Dutch word for slave (historical, political); in BDSM it denotes a consensual role implying deeper submission than 'onderdanige'; the word carries the full weight of Dutch colonial and Atlantic slave-trade history, which heightens its transgressive charge in kink use."}
{"term":"slavin","lang":"nl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"kink_paraphilia","subcategory":"bdsm_submissive","concept":"bdsm_submissive","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":50,"technical":10,"recognition_pct_current":96,"recognition_pct_peak":96,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Female slave; the grammatically feminine form of 'slaaf,' used in BDSM for a woman who has submitted fully to her dominant partner's authority.","english_term":"female slave","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Dutch feminine suffix '-in' marks the submissive's gender explicitly; in BDSM discourse the gendered form is deliberately chosen to foreground the woman's position within the dynamic; marginally higher crude score than 'slaaf' due to the added gendered-objectification dimension."}
{"term":"meesteres","lang":"nl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"kink_paraphilia","subcategory":"bdsm_dominant","concept":"bdsm_dominant_female","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":50,"technical":10,"recognition_pct_current":85,"recognition_pct_peak":85,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Mistress; a female dominant in a BDSM relationship who exercises authority and control over a submissive partner.","english_term":"mistress","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Formed from 'meester' (master) plus '-es,' the Dutch feminine suffix; genuinely polysemous — 'meesteres' also means schoolteacher (female) and skilled female practitioner — context fully disambiguates the BDSM meaning."}
