{"term":"spanking","lang":"nl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"kink_paraphilia","subcategory":"impact_play","concept":"impact_play","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"loanword","crude":60,"technical":15,"recognition_pct_current":78,"recognition_pct_peak":78,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Spanking; the erotic act of striking a partner's buttocks with an open hand or implement for arousal or discipline within BDSM.","english_term":"spanking","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"English loanword used unchanged in Dutch kink and mainstream sexual discourse; the native equivalent 'billenkoek geven' (to smack on the bottom) is strongly associated with child discipline rather than adult eroticism, driving adoption of the English term for the consensual adult practice."}
{"term":"handboeien","lang":"nl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"kink_paraphilia","subcategory":"bondage_restraint","concept":"bondage_restraint","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":35,"technical":15,"recognition_pct_current":97,"recognition_pct_peak":97,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Handcuffs; wrist restraints used in erotic BDSM bondage as well as in police and security contexts.","english_term":"handcuffs","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Compound of 'hand' and 'boeien' (shackles; also the verb meaning 'to captivate'); primary cultural association is law-enforcement, which provides plausible-deniability cover and keeps the crude score moderate; in erotic contexts often combined with 'fluweelzachte' (velvet-soft) to signal consensual play."}
